# Frame budget while scrolling continuously. "AGK perf" lines print every 50
# frames; the phases below are long enough that most 50-frame windows are
# purely one kind of work (see TECHNIQUE.md, "What it costs"):
#   ~150 frames idle, camera still
#   400 frames running right, 2 px/frame: the camera starts following at
#       x=153 (frame 60) and scrolls until it stops at 640 (frame 380)
#   300 frames walking left, 1 px/frame: camera scrolls back from 640 to 380
wait 148
press right+fire 400
press left 300
wait 2
expect-serial "x=532 cam=380"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 60
expect-no-serial "ERR|STACK SMASHED"
